# Shareable world settings. Values use Bash quoting (the file is sourced by Bash).
# The world's identity and other deployment details live in world.private.conf, which is read after this file (its
# keys win) and belongs in no shared or version-controlled copy of this directory. `dune-awakening init
# --display-name "..." --region "..."` writes it, deriving the unique name from your token's HostId:
#   WORLD_UNIQUE_NAME=sh-yourhostid-abcdef   (registered with Funcom on first start: never change it afterwards)
#   WORLD_DISPLAY_NAME=My\ Arrakis
#   WORLD_REGION=North\ America
# Add these to world.private.conf by hand when wanted:
#   EXTERNAL_ADDRESS=100.x.y.z   the address players connect to (default: the source address of this host's default
#                                route); use your Tailscale address (tailscale ip -4) when friends join over Tailscale
#   NOTIFY_TO=someone            who gets the weekly deep-idle notice and update notices
# Optional: idle frame-rate throttle (docs/operations.md, "Idle frame-rate throttle"). Defaults shown.
#IDLE_THROTTLE=1
#ACTIVE_FPS=20
#IDLE_FPS=5
#IDLE_AFTER=300
#DEEP_IDLE_FPS=1
#DEEP_IDLE_AFTER=86400
#IDLE_POLL=10
#DEEP_IDLE_POLL=30
#DEEP_IDLE_NOTICE=604800
# The post-compatible command that sends notices to NOTIFY_TO (absolute path).
#NOTIFY_CMD=/path/to/post
